========================
REACT COMPLETE ROADMAP
========================

1. WHAT IS REACT & WHY REACT
---------------------------
- React is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces.
- Developed by Facebook.
- Used for Single Page Applications (SPA).

Why React:
- Component-based architecture
- Reusable code
- Fast rendering using Virtual DOM
- Large community and ecosystem


2. INSTALL REACT (VITE)
----------------------
# Create React app using Vite
npm create vite@latest react-app
cd react-app
npm install
npm run dev

- Vite is fast and lightweight
- Better performance than CRA


3. IMPORT & EXPORT
-----------------
# Export
export default App;
export const title = "React";

# Import
import App from './App';
import { title } from './file';


4. REACT FOLDER STRUCTURE
------------------------
src/
 ├── components/
 ├── pages/
 ├── hooks/
 ├── services/
 ├── App.jsx
 ├── main.jsx

- Keeps project organized and scalable


5. REAL DOM VS VIRTUAL DOM
-------------------------
- Real DOM updates entire page (slow)
- Virtual DOM updates only changed elements
- React uses Virtual DOM for performance


6. JSX
------
- JSX = JavaScript + HTML
Example:
const element = <h1>Hello React</h1>;

- Makes UI code readable
- Converted to JS by Babel


7. useState HOOK
----------------
- Used to manage state in React

Example:
const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

- Updating state re-renders UI


8. ADDING CSS
-------------
Normal CSS:
import './App.css';

Tailwind CSS:
<button className="bg-blue-500 text-white px-4 py-2">
- Utility-first CSS framework
- Faster UI development


9. CALLING FUNCTIONS IN REACT
-----------------------------
Example:
<button onClick={handleClick}>Click</button>

- Used for events like click, submit, hover


10. FORM HANDLING
-----------------
Example:
<input
  value={name}
  onChange={(e) => setName(e.target.value)}
/>

- Controlled components
- Used in login, signup forms


11. TWO WAY BINDING
------------------
- State updates UI
- UI updates state
- Achieved using useState + onChange


12. COMPONENTS
--------------
- Reusable UI blocks

Example:
function Header() {
  return <h1>Header</h1>;
}

- Improves maintainability


13. PROPS DRILLING
------------------
- Passing data parent → child → grandchild

Example:
<Component data={value} />

Problem:
- Too many props

Solution:
- Context API
- Redux


14. RENDERING JSON DATA
----------------------
Example:
data.map(item => (
  <p key={item.id}>{item.name}</p>
))

- Used to display lists, tables, cards


15. API INTEGRATION (AXIOS)
--------------------------
npm install axios

Example:
axios.get(url)
  .then(res => setData(res.data))

- Used to connect frontend with backend


16. REACT ROUTER DOM
-------------------
npm install react-router-dom

- Used for routing without page reload
- Example routes:
  /login
  /dashboard
  /profile


17. REACT TOASTIFY
-----------------
- Used for flash messages

Example:
toast.success("Success!");
toast.error("Error!");

- Notifications and alerts


18. useEffect HOOK
------------------
- Handles side effects

Example:
useEffect(() => {
  fetchData();
}, []);

Used for:
- API calls
- Lifecycle events
- Subscriptions


19. useRef HOOK
---------------
- Direct DOM access
- Does not cause re-render

Example:
const inputRef = useRef();
inputRef.current.focus();


20. CONTEXT API
---------------
- Global state management
- Avoids props drilling

Used for:
- Authentication
- Theme
- User data


21. REDUX TOOLKIT
----------------
- Advanced global state management
- Centralized store
- Best for large applications


22. FRAMER MOTION
----------------
- Animation library for React

Example:
<motion.div animate={{ opacity: 1 }} />

- Smooth animations and transitions


23. DEPLOYMENT
--------------
npm run build

Platforms:
- Vercel
- Netlify
- GitHub Pages

========================
END OF REACT ROADMAP
========================
